      <h1 id="work-title">Engineering across systems, <em>infrastructure, and software.</em></h1>
      <p>ForgeWire Labs works across intelligent systems, distributed execution, developer infrastructure, local applications, communication, and technical education. Some of our projects connect; others stand on their own. Each addresses a distinct engineering problem with its own responsibilities and requirements.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="work-directions" aria-labelledby="work-directions-title">
      <div class="work-section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Engineering disciplines</p>
        <h2 id="work-directions-title">Where we work.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="work-card-grid">
        <article class="work-card work-glass">
          <h3>Intelligent systems</h3>
          <p>We build software that lets language models participate in complex, longer-running work without placing every responsibility on the model itself. ForgeWire explores provider-neutral orchestration, coordinated tools and agents, persistent context, and workflows that people can direct, inspect, and control.</p>
          <p class="work-card-project">Related work: <a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/ForgeWire-Overview">ForgeWire <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="work-card work-glass">
          <h3>Distributed computing &amp; execution</h3>
          <p>Moving work between machines involves more than connectivity. Tasks need authenticated dispatch, scoped authority, reliable execution state, and boundaries between the systems requesting work and those performing it. Fabric is our distributed execution effort built around those requirements.</p>
          <p class="work-card-project">Related work: <a href="{{ site.basePath }}/engineering/">Fabric <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="work-card work-glass">
          <h3>Developer &amp; repository infrastructure</h3>
          <p>Development produces more than code. Requirements, decisions, work items, constraints, and verification evidence matter to whoever continues the work. RepoPact keeps those records with the repository, where their relationships can be validated and their history retained across contributors and sessions.</p>
          <p class="work-card-project">Related work: <a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/repopact-core">RepoPact <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="work-card work-glass">
          <h3>Local applications &amp; planning</h3>
          <p>Not every engineering problem belongs inside an agent platform. Local planning benefits from structured records, clear ownership, and a distinction between organizing work and executing it. Anvil approaches those needs as a focused application with its own state and responsibilities.</p>
          <p class="work-card-project">Related work: <a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/anvil">Anvil <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="work-card work-glass">
          <h3>Communication &amp; coordination</h3>
          <p>Communication software has to account for channels, participants, continuity, and decisions that remain with people. Flink focuses on communication and coordination across connected systems while keeping those responsibilities distinct from an intelligent agent's internal workflow.</p>
          <p class="work-card-project">Related work: <a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/Flink">Flink <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="work-card work-glass">
          <h3>Technical education</h3>
          <p>Learning technical skills requires progression, practical exercises, useful feedback, and the ability to resume unfinished work. SkillForge Academy explores structured study, assessment, and practice in a learning environment built for continued development rather than isolated questions.</p>
          <p class="work-card-project">Related work: <a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/skillforge-academy">SkillForge Academy <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
        </article>
